  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The identity of X controls the nature and stability of the oxide scale in CrFeCoNiX alloys above 900 °C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al-containing CrFeCoNiX alloys form protective Al2O3 scales.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC6356250::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Si-containing CrFeCoNiX alloys form protective SiO2 scales.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6356250::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dense, continuous, adherent Al2O3 or SiO2 scales can protect alloys during high-temperature oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC6356250::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The protective character of Al2O3 and SiO2 is associated with high thermodynamic stability and low ionic diffusivity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6356250::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slower outward diffusion of Al or Si promotes formation of a continuous external protective scale.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower oxygen permeability associated with Al or Si produces compact scales with minimal internal stress.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6356250::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mn diffuses outward faster and is more reactive than Al or Si under the proposed exposure conditions.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mn-containing CrFeCoNiX alloys form thick, heterogeneous Mn-rich oxides and mixed spinel scales.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Volumetric mismatch and anisotropic thermal expansion in Mn-rich scales generate internal stress that causes cracking and spallation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6804173::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under identical exposure, Al- and Si-containing alloys will have thinner oxide layers than the Mn-containing alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC6356250::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under identical exposure, Al- and Si-containing alloys will have more coherent and adherent scales with fewer cracks and spallation events than the Mn-containing alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6356250::web::003::1_introduction",
        "PMC6804173::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mn-containing alloy is an unstable, spallation-prone baseline.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elevated-temperature exposure to a reactive environment causes oxide-scale development.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6804173::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed behavior applies generally above 900 °C in either oxidative or corrosive atmospheres and in both single- and multiphase CrFeCoNiX solid solutions.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC6356250::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxide structures in high-entropy alloys can vary with detailed chemistry, microstructure, surface heterogeneity, and phase instability.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using alloys that differ only in X, with similar processing histories and microstructures, provides the controlled comparison.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure of the Al- and Si-containing alloys to show thinner, more coherent, and better-adherent scales than the Mn-containing alloy would falsify the hypothesis.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment",
      "needs_support": false,
